        "title": "Electronics - Field Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Electronics is applied electromagnetism, reduced through successive approximations to tractable models — the same abstraction-layer strategy used in compiler theory (source → IR → machine code) or numerical analysis (exact PDE → finite element → algebraic system). The approximation hierarchy here is Maxwell's equations → quasi-static fields → lumped circuit elements (R, L, C), and the art of electronics is knowing when each layer breaks."
